From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Attribute callback stalls and passive ASGI body
 traffic

Why: control-beat misses coincide with local timeouts, but a post-delay stack and CPU-only scopes do not identify blocked callback wall time. The incident root remains unknown; this closes the attribution gap only.

Keep bounded >=500ms wall/inclusive-CPU records without adding inclusive CPU to residual totals. Emit only on the existing snapshot cadence. Count passive ASGI bytes and lifecycle outcomes with fixed safe route keys; global observation counters remain cumulative while per-route classification is deferred until response headers. No body drain, extra polling, live database fixtures, deployment, or production load.

Proof: callback suite RED (6 failures) before implementation; HTTP module RED and cumulative-delta regression RED (4 failures). GREEN: 312 tests across 18 files, 16 skips; final callback suite 8 tests. scripts/check all21 gates green. Isolated five-trial10000-operation fixture: no-op callback101ns plain/1725ns with existingCPU+wall; HTTP5byte streaming407ns plain/10635ns observed. Real controlled sleep snapshot wall0.5101s CPU0.000037s; consumed/sent5bytes. Schema, bounds, cadence and 30s-delta limitations documented in website/docs/developer-guide/stall-attribution.md. Incident owner retains live root correction and zero-local-timeout30min acceptance.
